-- 14_historical_seed_2026.sql
-- Historical backfill of real company records, Jan-Aug 2026, from clearmission_2026.xlsx
--
-- ASSUMPTIONS (confirmed with the business owner before this was generated):
--   1. Every historical job order is recorded as PAID IN FULL on its sale date
--      (invoice + one cash/bank payment + receipt, all same-day, outstanding = 0).
--   2. Line items are descriptive only: they do NOT reference inventory_item_id,
--      so this import does NOT deduct anything from your current live inventory stock.
--   3. Rows whose Size cell bundled more than one job (e.g. 'Flex/SAV' with two sizes)
--      had their Total split evenly across the sub-items; the original combined text
--      is kept in each item's remark for audit.
--   4. Customer names were de-duplicated by normalizing punctuation/case/whitespace only
--      (e.g. 'IB' and 'I.B.' merge) -- never by fuzzy-matching different name strings.
--   5. Payment method was not in the source data; every historical payment is recorded
--      as 'Cash' unless you tell me otherwise and I regenerate this file.
--   6. Monthly expense totals you gave me (no day/category breakdown available) were
--      split across standard categories and random days within each month as an
--      ESTIMATE ONLY -- every generated expense row's remark says so.
--
-- ASSUMED COLUMN NAMES: this script is written against the schema as I built it earlier
-- in this project. If any statement below errors with 'column ... does not exist' or
-- similar, paste me the error (same way we fixed earlier schema-load errors) and I will
-- adjust just this file -- nothing else needs to change.
--
-- Safe to re-run: every insert is guarded with NOT EXISTS, so running this twice will
-- not create duplicates.

